    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>More Information on the Return Values of the SDK Functions.</para>
<para>Most of the SDK functions return a <ref refid="group__cuvis__returns_1gaa06c62ba25240f4763da0e590ebf3b9d" kindref="member">cuvis_status_t</ref>. This value indicates if the function call was executed sucessfully or if a error occurred. If the value is <ref refid="group__cuvis__returns_1ggaa06c62ba25240f4763da0e590ebf3b9da405da0d107497b3596a3818a48478c9f" kindref="member">status_error</ref> for example, this indicates that an error occurred. The specific error message can then be retrieved via <ref refid="group__cuvis__returns_1ga3b39f3a4e8390f24066d28acb0e6bff2" kindref="member">cuvis_get_last_error_msg</ref> to get more details. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
